{
  "task_id": "crystallographic-wyckoff-position-analysis",
  "top_k": 5,
  "requirements": [
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_b22f79a88d03e7e8a319",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/crystallographic-wyckoff-position-analysis/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 1,
        "line_end": 1,
        "exact_text": "You are a materials science researcher. You want to analyze the crystal structure of a few samples. You are given a few CIF files generated by SHELX through X-ray Diffraction.\n",
        "source_sha256": "f9edf58cc8ffde5545c1ffa43a043a1ef74f125ed87bd16fb1ed48ae10b326c8",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_3bed3eb35b2ef19c12ac",
      "requirement_type": "ARTIFACT",
      "criticality": "HARD",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/crystallographic-wyckoff-position-analysis/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 3,
        "line_end": 3,
        "exact_text": "To process the given CIF file data in batches, you are required to build a function in python to analyze Wyckoff position multiplicities and calculate approximate coordinates for the first atom of each Wyckoff position.\n",
        "source_sha256": "f9edf58cc8ffde5545c1ffa43a043a1ef74f125ed87bd16fb1ed48ae10b326c8",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_b1168cca806a55cc9fcb",
      "requirement_type": "OUTPUT_PATH",
      "criticality": "HARD",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/crystallographic-wyckoff-position-analysis/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 10,
        "line_end": 10,
        "exact_text": "An example output of using input \"/root/cif_files/FeS2_mp-226.cif\" (datasource: https://next-gen.materialsproject.org/) shall look like as follows in dict format (for fractions, constrain fractions to have denominators ≤ 12 for a simpler result):\n",
        "source_sha256": "f9edf58cc8ffde5545c1ffa43a043a1ef74f125ed87bd16fb1ed48ae10b326c8",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_e11c9c74ae2f8bae34dc",
      "requirement_type": "ARTIFACT",
      "criticality": "HARD",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/crystallographic-wyckoff-position-analysis/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 25,
        "line_end": 26,
        "exact_text": "You are encouraged to use external imports for CIF file reading, Wyckoff position multiplicity calculations, and coordinate calculations for the first atom of each Wyckoff position.\nYou must not hardcode answers within your script.\n",
        "source_sha256": "f9edf58cc8ffde5545c1ffa43a043a1ef74f125ed87bd16fb1ed48ae10b326c8",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_9a727ab579d736ad9e96",
      "requirement_type": "OUTPUT_PATH",
      "criticality": "HARD",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/crystallographic-wyckoff-position-analysis/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 28,
        "line_end": 28,
        "exact_text": "The coordinated calculated should be rounded to the closest rational number format, as shown in example output.\n",
        "source_sha256": "f9edf58cc8ffde5545c1ffa43a043a1ef74f125ed87bd16fb1ed48ae10b326c8",
